add('What did the early discrete peak classes suggest?','EXPLORATORY','The first pass separated peaks by the signs of construct enrichment.',findings=['Strict opposite-quadrant classes contained 224 324-biased and 3,024 328-biased peaks.','The selected classes emphasized 328-associated binding.','The class definition conditions on noisy, sparse enrichment estimates.'],changed='The striking imbalance needed a selection-independent check.',ids=['SEL-STRICT'],foot='N = 224 vs 3,024 selected peaks. Mean-CPM log ratios, pseudocount 0.5.',sign=True)
